      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Find $x$, if $4a+3x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+3x & =b \\\\ 3x & =b-4a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(b-4a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
